  "description": "The so-called \"House of the Tiles\" at Lerna belongs to the Korakou culture in the Early Helladic II period (ca. 2500\u20132300 BCE). It was a monumental two-story building (12 x 25 meters) and has been interpreted as either a \"proto-palace\" or administrative center.",
